      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In nowadays the wide propagation of surgical treatment of metabolic syndrome using the laparoscopic gastro-bypass surgery can be explained hy severe consequences of clinical manifestation of metabolic syndrome. The risk of the mentioned method has to be clear-cut assessed. The comprehensive analysis of changes in indicators of metabolism has to be applied to patients with metabolic syndrome before and after laparoscopic gastro-bypass surgery. The study was carried out on the sampling of 41 patients, 16 patients before and 25 after laparoscopic gastro-bypass surgery. In patients with metabolic syndrome after laparoscopic gastro-bypass surgery the normalization of concentration of glucose and glycated hemoglobin was established. The level of triglycerides, low density lipoproteins and reactive protein reliably decreased as compared with indicators of in non-operated patients. After laparoscopic gastro-bypass surgery, the positive dynamics of activity of enzymes of blood serum was noted."},
